# The safe Petitboot entry's arguments: walnut-safe on dev_hdd1 (ps3-hdd1-boot), <release>-safe in a root's
# /etc/kboot.conf (ps3-update-kboot), and the installers' first menus (tools/ssdimg/stamp.py, walnut-install
# usb as walnut-usb-safe), all from this one file. They go at the end of that entry, after the kernel's own,
# so they win: conservative settings for a boot that fails with the defaults. The safe entry boots the same
# kernel and initramfs as the default one. Arguments are separated by spaces or lines; # starts a comment
# that runs to the line's end. Only letters, digits and _ . , : = / + - are allowed in an argument; a word
# with anything else is left out by every writer, with a message.
#
# lv1's shared SPE (the 7th) off: our kernels' args turn it on (docs/SPU.md)
spu_base.enum_shared=0
